{
  "id": "PPA-09",
  "title": "Phytohormone Networks & Crosstalk",
  "subtitle": "Core biosynthetic modules and derepression signaling circuits for Auxin, ABA, JA, GA, and Ethylene",
  "caption": "Integrated plant hormone networks. Compares the parallel derepression logic of the major phytohormones: (1) Auxin perception by SCFTIR1 triggering Aux/IAA degradation and ARF release; (2) Abscisic acid (ABA) binding to PYR/PYL/RCARs relieving PP2C inhibition of SnRK2 kinases; (3) Jasmonate-isoleucine (JA-Ile) mediated SCFCOI1 destruction of JAZ repressors freeing MYC2; and (4) Gibberellin (GA) and Ethylene circuits regulating DELLA degradation and EIN2/EIN3 transcriptional activation.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
